---
import BaseLayout from "../../../shared/components/BaseLayout.astro";
import { MAIN_SITE_URL } from "../../../shared/config/config";

const OPERATOR_INFO = "{OPERATOR-INFO}";
const OPERATOR_EMAIL = "{OPERATOR-EMAIL}";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  name: "Privacy Policy",
  url: MAIN_SITE_URL + "/privacy-policy/",
  description: "This platform is static: no accounts, no tracking, no cookies. Your data stays yours.",
  isPartOf: { "@type": "WebSite", "name": "Porn Recovery Knowledge Platform", "url": "https://selfcontrolatlas.com" },
};
---
<BaseLayout
  siteTitle="Porn Recovery Knowledge Platform"
  siteUrl={MAIN_SITE_URL}
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="This platform is static: no accounts, no tracking, no cookies. Your data stays yours."
  canonical="/privacy-policy/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Home", url: "/" }, { name: "Privacy Policy", url: "/privacy-policy/" }]}
>
<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p>This website is a static educational platform. This policy explains, in plain terms,
how information is — and is not — handled here. It is written to be read by a person, not
just a lawyer. If you have questions after reading it, contact <strong>{OPERATOR_EMAIL}</strong>.</p>
<p><strong>Last updated: 2026-10-23</strong></p>

<h2>1. Who operates this site</h2>
<p>This site is operated by:</p>
<p><strong>{OPERATOR_INFO}</strong></p>
<p>Contact: <strong>{OPERATOR_EMAIL}</strong></p>

<h2>2. The short version</h2>
<p>This site collects <strong>no personal data</strong>. There are no accounts, no sign-ups,
no analytics, no trackers, and no cookies. The only browser-side persistence is an optional
journal tool that keeps your entries on your own device. If you want the details, read on;
if you want the summary, that is it.</p>

<h2>3. What this site does not do</h2>
<p>This site is deliberately minimal about data. It does <strong>not</strong>:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Create accounts.</strong> There is no sign-up, no login, and no user profile system.</li>
  <li><strong>Collect personal data.</strong> We do not collect names, email addresses, phone numbers, or any other personally identifying information.</li>
  <li><strong>Run analytics or tracking.</strong> The site runs no analytics scripts, no third-party trackers, and no fingerprinting.</li>
  <li><strong>Serve advertising.</strong> There is no ad network and no ad-related data processing. See the <a href="/advertising-disclosure/">Advertising Disclosure</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>Set cookies.</strong> This site does not set cookies. See the <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p>Because none of these are present, there is no personal data for us to store, sell,
share, or process.</p>

<h2>4. Data we do not have — by category</h2>
<p>For clarity, here is how the site treats the most common categories of data:</p>
<table class="data-table">
  <thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Collected?</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Names / email / phone</td><td><strong>No</strong></td><td>No forms collect identifying contact details.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Account / login</td><td><strong>No</strong></td><td>No account system exists.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Location</td><td><strong>No</strong></td><td>No geolocation and no IP-based profiling.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Device / browser data</td><td><strong>No</strong></td><td>No fingerprinting or device profiling.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Behavioral / browsing history</td><td><strong>No</strong></td><td>No tracking scripts or analytics.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Payment / financial</td><td><strong>No</strong></td><td>Nothing is sold; no payment data is processed.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Health or sensitive data</td><td><strong>No</strong></td><td>No intake forms or questionnaires.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Communications</td><td><strong>No</strong></td><td>No on-site messaging, comments, or forms.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>5. Browser-local tools</h2>
<p>The optional <a href="/tools/trigger-journal/">Trigger Journal</a> tool stores your entries
<strong>only in your own browser's local storage</strong>:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Entries never leave your device.</li>
  <li>Entries are never transmitted to any server.</li>
  <li>Entries are deleted when you clear your browser data.</li>
  <li>We have no access to them, ever.</li>
</ul>
<p>This is a privacy-preserving design choice: the tool is useful without any data leaving
your machine. Local storage is similar to a cookie in that it lives in your browser, but it
is used here only to keep your own entries on your own device.</p>

<h2>6. Server logs and hosting</h2>
<p>Like most websites, the hosting infrastructure may keep minimal, transient server logs
(for example, to prevent abuse, maintain security, or diagnose outages). These logs may
include technical information such as an IP address, user agent, or timestamp. These logs
are:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Not used to build profiles of individual visitors.</li>
  <li>Not combined with any other data about you.</li>
  <li>Not sold or shared for advertising.</li>
  <li>Retained only as long as operationally necessary.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not use server logs to identify individual users or to track their reading.</p>

<h2>7. Content sources and de-identification</h2>
<p>Community-derived content on this site is <strong>de-identified before publication</strong>:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Original usernames, identifiers, contact details, and locations are never published.</li>
  <li>De-identification is performed following the rules in the <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p>This means the site does not republish personal information about the people whose
experiences inform its content. The goal is that no reader can identify the person behind
an experience.</p>

<h2>8. Third-party links</h2>
<p>Pages may link to external websites — research publishers, official classifications, or
crisis services. Those sites have their own privacy practices, which we do not control.
When you leave this site, you are subject to the privacy policy of the site you visit. We
link to external resources for reference; we do not transmit data to them on your behalf,
and we do not embed their trackers or scripts.</p>

<h2>9. Children's privacy</h2>
<p>This site is intended for adults and is not directed to children under 13. We do not
knowingly collect personal information from children of any age, because we do not collect
personal information at all. If you are a parent or guardian and believe your child has
submitted information to this site, contact <strong>{OPERATOR_EMAIL}</strong> — although,
given the site's design, no such information would be stored.</p>

<h2>10. Legal bases and jurisdiction</h2>
<p>Because the site does not collect or process personal data, most data-protection
obligations (such as GDPR data-subject rights or CCPA/CPRA access and deletion requests)
have no personal data to act on. To the extent any data processing occurs — for example,
transient server logs — it is:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Governed by the law of the jurisdiction of the operator stated in section 1.</li>
  <li>Processed on the basis of legitimate operational necessity (security, stability, and abuse prevention).</li>
</ul>

<h2>11. Your rights</h2>
<p>Even though the site collects no personal data, you retain the rights available under
your local law, which may include the right to access, correct, or delete personal data,
and the right to object to or restrict processing. If you believe any personal data about
you appears on the site, contact <strong>{OPERATOR_EMAIL}</strong> and we will investigate
and, where applicable, correct or remove it.</p>
<p>Because there are no accounts and no data collection, there is no automated way to
exercise these rights; they are handled by contacting us directly.</p>

<h2>12. Data retention</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Personal data:</strong> none is collected, so none is retained.</li>
  <li><strong>Server logs:</strong> retained only as long as operationally necessary, then deleted.</li>
  <li><strong>Trigger Journal entries:</strong> stored only in your browser; deleted when you clear your browser data. We never see or retain them.</li>
</ul>

<h2>13. International users</h2>
<p>The site is accessible worldwide, but it collects no personal data from any location.
Where transient server logs exist, they are processed in accordance with this policy
regardless of where you access the site from.</p>

<h2>14. Security</h2>
<p>Because the site collects no personal data, there is no database of user data to breach.
We still take reasonable measures to keep the site itself secure and stable. The most
important privacy protection here is architectural: the less data the site collects, the
less there is to protect.</p>

<h2>15. Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted on this page, and the "Last
updated" date above will be revised. Material changes will be highlighted. Because the site
collects no data and has no accounts, we cannot email you about changes — the current
version is always the one published here.</p>

<h2>16. Frequently asked questions</h2>
<p><strong>Does this site use cookies?</strong> No. See the <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a>.</p>
<p><strong>Can I delete my data?</strong> There is no account and no stored personal data to delete. If you use the Trigger Journal, clearing your browser data removes your entries from your own device.</p>
<p><strong>Does this site sell my data?</strong> No. It collects no data and sells nothing. See the <a href="/advertising-disclosure/">Advertising Disclosure</a>.</p>
<p><strong>Does this site track me?</strong> No. There are no analytics or tracking scripts.</p>
<p><strong>What if I see my personal information on the site?</strong> Contact <strong>{OPERATOR_EMAIL}</strong> and we will investigate and remove it.</p>

<h2>17. Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about privacy can be directed to:</p>
<p><strong>{OPERATOR_EMAIL}</strong></p>
<p>or via the project repository: <code>https://github.com/martinxionbiotech-max/jiese/issues</code>.</p>
<p>Related documents: <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a>,
<a href="/advertising-disclosure/">Advertising Disclosure</a>,
<a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
